ices for research, biotechnology development and production, and pharmaceutical drug therapy development and production.\nL359: \nL360: 【39†Sigma-Aldrich^{®} Solutions】【40†BioReliance^{®} Solutions】【41†Millipore^{®} Solutions】【42†SAFC^{®} Solutions】【43†Milli-Q^{®} Solutions】【44†Supelco^{®} Solutions】\nL361: © 2026 Merck KGaA, Darmstadt, Germany and/or its affiliates. All Rights Reserved, including Text and Data Mining for AI training and similar technologies.\nL362: \nL363: Reproduction of any materials from the site is strictly forbidden without permission.\nL364: \nL365: 【45†Site Use Terms】|【46†Privacy Policy】|【47†General Terms and Conditions of Sale】|【48†Copyright Consent】 |【49†Site Map】\nL366: \nL367: An unknown error has occured.\nL368:   * 2026-08-10T06:00+00:00\nL369:   * bvseo_fps, prod_bvrr, vn_firebird_3.1.50\nL370:   * cp_1, bvpage1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCell line designation: IAL-TND1 (https://www.ars.usda.gov/SP2UserFiles/person/3489/TND1.pdf)\nciteturn34view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ars.usda.gov/SP2UserFiles/person/3489/TND1.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 33\nL0@P0: Cell line designation: IAL-TND1\nL1@P0: Tissue source: Trichoplusia ni imaginal wing discs\nL2@P0: Date initiated: November 5, 1979\nL3@P0: Morphology: Originally cells grew as epithelial cells\nL4@P0: in vesicles, currently are available only as\nL5@P0: multicellular aggregates (although see Lynn et al., In\nL6@P0: Vitro Cell. Dev. Biol. 21:277-281 (1985))\nL7@P0: Karyology: near diploid at low passage\nL8@P0: Culture medium: Ex-Cell 420 with 5% (v/v) heat\nL9@P0: inactivated fetal bovine serum\nL10@P0: (available from JRH Biosciences,\nL11@P0: Lenexa, KS)\nL12@P0: Alternatively, modified TNM-FH which contains:\nL13@P0: 100 ml Grace's (available from GIBCO, JRH Biosciences, SIGMA & other companies)\nL14@P0: 0.3 g T. C. Yeastolate\nL15@P0: 0.3 g Lactalbumin hydrolysate\nL16@P0:  10 ml Fetal bovine serum\nL17@P0: pH should be about 6.2 and osmolarity 350 mOsm/kg.\nL18@P0: TNM-FH is available from:\nL19@P0: GIBCO (Grace's Insect Cell Culture Medium, Supplemented = cat. # 11605-011)\nL20@P0: SIGMA (TNM-FH Insect Medium = cat. # T3285)\nL21@P0: JRH Biosciences (Hink's TNM-FH Insect Medium = cat. # 51-94278)\nL22@P0: (These are the liquid formulations. Some manufacturers also supply them as dry powders that\nL23@P0: are less expensive but require more preparation time. None of these products contain fetal\nL24@P0: bovine serum.)\nL25@P0: Subculture procedure: Vesicles or clumps disrupted by gentle pipetting. Centrifuge at low speed.\nL26@P0: Discard old medium and resuspend into fresh. Currently cells are split at ~1:15 weekly.\nL27@P0: Comments: Vesicles change morphologically and biochemically in response to 20-hydroxyecdysone.\nL28@P0: Cultures spontaneously changed to aggregates after a year in culture but can be changed back to\nL29@P0: vesicles with hemolymph.\nL30@P0: Reference: Lynn, D. E., S. G. Miller, and H. Oberlander 1982. Proc. Natl. Acad Sci USA 79: 2589-2593.\nL31@P0: Distribution of cell lines from the Insect Biocontrol Laboratory requires a material transfer agreement\nL32@P0: between the recipient’s organization and the Agricultural Research Service.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDaigo's IMK Medium・398-01333・392-01331[Detail Information] | [Life Science][Cell Culture]|Laboratory Chemicals-FUJIFILM Wako Pure Chemical Corporation (https://labchem-wako.fujifilm.com/us/product/detail/W01N0139-0133.html)\nciteturn34view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://labchem-wako.fujifilm.com/us/product/detail/W01N0139-0133.html\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 177\nL0: [Input][Input] 【0†iframe†www.googletagmanager.com】\nL1: \nL2: This site may not be displayed pro